{
    "pr_body": "Initial implementation for outputting a summary of actions ran\r\nwhen using RemoteSpawnRunner. Breaks down by cached/uncached and\r\nlocal vs non-local.\r\n\r\nCurrently it surfaces a number of local steps that are for Bazel's\r\nbookkeeping: I've seen CreateRunfiles, though there could be more\r\nin that category. As a follow up, we need to decide what to do about\r\nthose: users would expect to see 100% remote execution if everything\r\nis working properly.\r\n\r\nRELNOTES: Bazel now adds action summary statistics when using remote execution.\r\nFIXES: #2846",
    "original_commit_id": "cf097e464bbe2f9ff40ba0f70f2425033c14cefb",
    "merged": false,
    "pr_number": 4531,
    "pr_title": "remote: output stats on each run",
    "lang": "java",
    "full_name": "bazelbuild/bazel",
    "pr_comment": [
        "I'm not sure that this is the right approach - maybe it makes more sense to have all SpawnRunner implementations return stats, and then aggregate and print them at a higher level? That'll also include stats about local execution and whatnot, which seems like a good thing in general.",
        "friendly ping :)",
        "I agree that this should be re-engineered to make it more general.\r\nI'm reading through the architecture to figure out the best way of doing it.",
        "Can this be closed?",
        "Does the Build Event Protocol already produce the data we need? It's not essential that it's printed in the terminal output.",
        "@alexeagle no it unfortunately doesn't (but it will). @agoulti is working on this but took a different approach as in this PR IIUC.",
        "Are there any updates? Can we import this PR until there's a better long-term solution? Can we close it otherwise?",
        "The other approach is almost ready to submit. I've been busy with other things but I'm planning on submitting a new version next week."
    ],
